ado  you do see some older folks moving out  of california  but it's really no big deal the  percentage of californians who plan to  leave the state  when you ask them has remained basically  the same over the last two years  23 of california california voters say i  am seriously considering leaving the  state  that was 24 2 years ago basically the  same  that sounds huge and obviously if a  quarter of california left  california it would be a cataclysm  economically  but remember that most people who say  they're considering leaving don't i mean  i've been considering moving to miami  for five years and then i realize  i don't really know anybody there i'd be  far from my family  i'm gonna stay put at least for now but  like if you ask me at many points  i i would consider leaving and going to  florida sure yeah  that's something i've considered not  really going to do it and that's for  most people  one interesting thing is that there's a  big partisan gap though on that question  if you ask democrats 21 say i'm  considering leaving california  if you ask republicans 30 percent say  i'm considering leaving california  no surprise politically it's very and  vogue right now to say  you're thinking of leaving california  any guys  i'll do it don't make me because i'm  just one day from  renting a u-haul and getting out of here  most people don't do it  and it's important to remember that if  people did leave california in large  numbers the heroic  perfect market that the republicans love  to harp on  would lead to lower prices that's what  republicans claim is the problem in  california they say prices are too high  a real estate costs too much rent is too  damn high  that's caused by demand there's a reason  it's more expensive to live in san  francisco than it is to live in  you know tulsa oklahoma no offense to  oklahoma  education is better in california  there are higher salaries in california  than in oklahoma there's more access to  culture  there's more access to airports with  direct flights to the rest of the world  there's a higher standard of healthcare  there's better infrastructure it  demand drives prices up doesn't mean  people in oklahoma are bad people  it's just the market that these right  wingers point to  that's why it's expensive to be in  california but  right wingers just feel like everybody's  leaving california  so do we pay attention to fats or do we  pay attention to feelings i forget how  that statement goes  over time people may leave california  who knows but it's just not happening  right now  to any significant degree california's  not failing economically  and people are not fleeing california  that's the truth  it may change in the future but it's not  happening right now
 

